", "x0": 0.1912087912087912, "y0": 0.5322455322455323, "x1": 0.8021978021978022, "y1": 0.5446775446775447}, {"text": "Draw a graph of prices as a function of time that fits this description.", "x0": 0.189010989010989, "y0": 0.5485625485625486, "x1": 0.7098901098901099, "y1": 0.560994560994561}, {"text": "(4) A ball is dropped from a height of 2 metres onto a hard floor and bounces.", "x0": 0.14395604395604394, "y0": 0.5982905982905983, "x1": 0.8021978021978022, "y1": 0.6107226107226107}, {"text": "After each bounce, the maximum height reached by the ball is 75% of the", "x0": 0.189010989010989, "y0": 0.6146076146076146, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.627039627039627}, {"text": "previous maximum height. Thus, after it first hits the floor, it reaches a height", "x0": 0.189010989010989, "y0": 0.6223776223776224, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.6472416472416472}, {"text": "of 1-5 metres before falling again, and after the second bounce, it reaches a", "x0": 0.1879120879120879, "y0": 0.6464646464646465, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.6588966588966589}, {"text": "height of 1-125 metres before falling again.", "x0": 0.189010989010989, "y0": 0.662004662004662, "x1": 0.5153846153846153, "y1": 0.6744366744366744}, {"text": "(i) What is the maximum height reached after the third bounce?", "x0": 0.2076923076923077, "y0": 0.6954156954156954, "x1": 0.7054945054945055, "y1": 0.7078477078477079}, {"text": "(ii) What kind of sequence is formed by the successive maximum heights?", "x0": 0.2032967032967033, "y0": 0.7296037296037297, "x1": 0.789010989010989, "y1": 0.7420357420357421}, {"text": "(iii) What is the total distance travelled by the ball from the time it was first", "x0": 0.1978021978021978, "y0": 0.7637917637917638, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.7762237762237763}, {"text": "dropped until it eventually comes to rest on the floor?", "x0": 0.24505494505494504, "y0": 0.7801087801087802, "x1": 0.6494505494505495, "y1": 0.7925407925407926}], [{"text": "QUESTION 6. Us