de of 20 squares with a common corner, as shown in the diagram.", "x0": 0.189010989010989, "y0": 0.6752136752136753, "x1": 0.8021978021978022, "y1": 0.6876456876456877}, {"text": "The odd-numbered \u2018stripes\u2019 between successive squares are shaded in the", "x0": 0.1879120879120879, "y0": 0.6907536907536908, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.7031857031857032}, {"text": "diagram. The shaded stripes are painted in gold paint, which costs $9 per square", "x0": 0.1879120879120879, "y0": 0.7062937062937062, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.7195027195027195}, {"text": "centimetre.", "x0": 0.1879120879120879, "y0": 0.7241647241647242, "x1": 0.2703296703296703, "y1": 0.7319347319347319}, {"text": "The side length of the nth square is (2n+4) cm. The nth stripe lies between", "x0": 0.1879120879120879, "y0": 0.7544677544677545, "x1": 0.8032967032967033, "y1": 0.7684537684537684}, {"text": "the nth square and the square.", "x0": 0.1879120879120879, "y0": 0.7715617715617715, "x1": 0.4912087912087912, "y1": 0.7839937839937839}, {"text": "(i) Show that the area of the nth stripe is (8 +20) cm?.", "x0": 0.2076923076923077, "y0": 0.8026418026418026, "x1": 0.6505494505494506, "y1": 0.8181818181818182}, {"text": "(ii) Hence find the areas of the first and last stripes.", "x0": 0.2032967032967033, "y0": 0.8414918414918415, "x1": 0.6032967032967033, "y1": 0.853923853923854}, {"text": "(iii) Hence find the total cost of the gold paint for the logo.", "x0": 0.1978021978021978, "y0": 0.8756798756798757, "x1": 0.6538461538461539, "y1": 0.8881118881118881}], [{"text": "QUESTION 7. Use a separate Writing Booklet. Marks", "x0": 0.14395604395604394, "y0": 0.0979020979020979, "x1": 0.8703296703296703, "y1": 0.11577311577311578}, {"text": "(a) sec@ and tan@ in terms of sin@ and cos@, show that 2", "x0": 0.14395604395604394, "y0": 0.12742812742812742, "x1": 0.8703296703296703, "y1": 0.13986013986013987}, {"text": "sec? @\u2014tan?@=1.", "x0": 0.4021978021978022, "y0": 0.1561771561771562, "x